# Accepted vulnerabilities, reviewed and justified.
#
# Every entry needs a CVE id, why it does not apply, and a date to revisit. An unexplained
# suppression is indistinguishable from an unnoticed one.
#
# The CI gate already skips unfixed CVEs (nothing to action until Red Hat ships a fix); those are
# reported by the weekly scan of the published image instead. So this file is only for a FIXABLE
# HIGH/CRITICAL that genuinely does not apply here.
#
# Example:
#   # CVE-2025-00000 — glibc, reachable only via a setuid path. The plugin runs as UID 1001 and
#   # serves static files; there is no setuid binary in the image. Revisit 2026-12-01.
#   CVE-2025-00000
